{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You will find</b> — this is supernal kindness that HaShem says to David: Your hand will find, and it is the left, and likewise her hands will send forth to the peg." "And the meaning of <b>you will find</b> — like the way of 'and I shall press them' [2 Samuel 22:38], so that those who shoot may find them. And the meaning: they will not be able to flee and to separate and to escape."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:03.806358859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}